   $q$In paragraph 1, the author says a glacier "looks like a frozen giant sleeping on a mountainside." What does this comparison suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A glacier is a creature that wakes up in the spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"A glacier moves quickly when no one is watching it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A glacier is small enough to fit in a mountain cave.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"A glacier is huge and appears to be completely still.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A glacier is huge and appears to be completely still.$q$, $q$A giant is very large, and a sleeping person lies still, which matches the next sentence: "It seems perfectly still." The glacier is not a real creature; the comparison describes how it looks.$q$, 'draft', '92e5ae9d-69d4-57d8-bd18-4c93d44f09b4')
