   $q$In paragraph 4, pigeons may be "reading the land below like a map." What does this simile suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Pigeons ignore the ground and fly only by sound.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Pigeons carry small paper maps tied to their legs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Pigeons use features they see on the ground to guide their flight.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Pigeons can read words printed on road signs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Pigeons use features they see on the ground to guide their flight.$q$, $q$The sentence says pigeons "remember landmarks such as rivers and roads," so they use the ground the way a person uses a map. The notes tied to their legs were messages, not maps.$q$, 'draft', '1f1ed3c4-411a-5394-b541-ca3671e3ad70')
